  "notes": "Drawn from 2025-2026 photos of A321neos and an A330neo. The fin's white sweep is painted as one artwork seen through the fin: trailing half at the tip on the left side, leading half on the right (mirrored false). The bird's head faces forward on both sides. The belly is seen only obliquely: the yellow is taken to run under the whole fuselage, and the belly title's exact place and size are approximate. Exact brand colors are not published; all colors by eye. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on RP-C4121 (left, from below; placed between the forward and aft doors): the title runs about x 0.14 to 0.40, starting just aft of the forward door (lowercase 0.72 of the ascenders); the belly title about as long (0.25, low). RP-C4125's right side is too far off and too blurred to measure. The yellow's waving edge, the bird's sweeps and the fin's white sweep are curves: smooth.",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximation. The 2015 livery replaced the 2005 scheme (white with yellow and blue); RP-C4101, the last aircraft in it, left the fleet in September 2026."
